      "tags": [
        "Classic"
      ],
      "description": "In 2011, Dark Souls let players praise the sun, and that sun cast a shadow long enough to engulf the whole industry. The action-RPG–boosted by its spiritual predecessor, Demon’s Souls–kickstarted a new subgenre with a refreshing level of boldness that made it unignorable for any developer making a game with a sword. It was a paradigm shift that swallowed the action genre and meant almost everything was molded after Dark Souls and its stamina meter, methodical movement, and esoteric world. Even with small deviations here and there, there was seemingly little room for action games unwilling to stick to this blueprint.\n\nThis dearth of variety is precisely what makes Onimusha: Way of the Sword so refreshing. Instead of capitulating to trends, Capcom’s latest hit bravely demonstrates a level of versatility action games should have had all this time in this post-Dark Souls world.\n\n",
